            <title>[LU-20398] An error message should pop up when adding an LNet interface if invalid values are provided for conns_per_peer</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20398</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;created lustre server instance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;deleted the default network during GCP provision&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;add net work using following command along with conns_per_peer:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lnetctl net add --net tcp --if eth0 --conns-per-peer=1000000000000000000000000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;expected error message&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;checked number conns_per_peer with lnetctl net show -v command:&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
found with maximum value 65535&lt;/p&gt;

